{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1335896-sphere-help","id":1335896,"title":"sphere help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-09-15T08:17:29-07:00","id":1335896,"title":"sphere help","content":"<span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Hello everyone, it is time for me to make my very first post here after some time of silent participation and observation. I have just started a game of Mage the Ascension and I already love the setting and my character. I find the magic system quite challenging while at the same time super interesting with a lot of depth. I think that I could need some help and inspiration however how to use and fuse the various spheres for interesting results and usage. My character is a Dreamspeaker that deals a lot of therapeutic counseling and support for people in crisis and suffering various forms of trauma (supernaturally based as well as the more mundane). </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">Her sphere mastery so far is; Spirit 2, Mind 2 and Prime 2. </span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\">My question is basically just asking for advice and inspiration for how I could use these spheres in a creative manner to help her in her professional role as well as just generally surviving in the world of darkness. I know that all 3 spheres in general serve as more supportive and non-combat based roles, which is okay since she is not much of a fighter (she knows how to use a gun for when self defense becomes necessary) but I still struggle to come up with actual applications and rotes for the spheres. </span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25626-eiryth","name":"Eiryth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25626_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T12:22:07-07:00","id":1335931,"title":"","content":"Mind 2 can be used to change emotions/emotional responses but it generally isn't long term, so you can't really make long term changes in people via Mind but you could bolster your therapy methods by giving off the emotion of calm.<br /> <br /> Spirit 2 can be used to actually communicate with spirits so you could ask spirits of healing/nice spirits to watch over people.<br /> <br /> Prime 2 can let you shoot kamehamehas so theres always that","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25315,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","user":"Jihelu","date":". 09-15-2019, 03:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-15T14:36:43-07:00","id":1335946,"title":"","content":"Mind 1 and 2 have a lot of applications for boosting a therapists mundane actions, even if not skipping over things or using magic to heal things quickly (that's higher level stuff). Mind 1 lets you temporarily boost your Social and Mental Attributes, perform Aura scans to determine emotional states, and so on. Mind 2, as noted already, can help adjust a patient's current emotional state to help keep treatment sessions on track.<br /> <br /> Prime 1 lets you sense if any of their emotional trauma is a normal response to seeing something that should not have been seen, or if there's a supernatural effect involved. Prime 2 (and possibly Mind as well) would assist in unraveling a supernaturally implanted mental trauma (aka undo a power that inflicts a Derangement on a character).<br /> <br /> Spirit 1, like Prime 1, would help you spot if a spirit is partially to blame because they're connected to the patient somehow. Mage has some funky rules for dealing with ghosts/wraiths specifically if you don't take certain Merits, but you'd at least be able to gather some clues along those lines. Spirit 2 would let you talk to spirits attached (and present) to the patient, and there's a chance you might be able to help them to stop negatively impacting your client's mental health. And as noted you can ask friendly spirits to help out as Spirit 2 (though spirits in the WoD are highly transactional, even if they are inclined to help, they need to be shown proper respect and offerings before they will unless you have a standing pact with them...which generally takes higher Spirit for a mage to codify on their own, don't think of Spirit 2 as an unlimited source of helpers).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T12:48:03-07:00","id":1336082,"title":"","content":"Once you raise your Prime to 3 you can get Quintessence from spirits, though usually it's best to get their permission first.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T13:28:14-07:00","id":1336085,"title":"","content":"One of the big things that slow down therapy is the tendency for patients to keep things back. Whether that's talking about events they've experienced/witnessed, personal anxieties, or thoughts they think are shameful. Mind 1 can allow the character to sense when the patient is holding back, a useful tool for helping them resolve issues. At Mind 2, the character can read the person's surface thoughts, getting a better insight into what, exactly, the patient is not saying. Mind 3 is needed to dig deeper, to explore buried anxieties.<br /> <br /> Obviously, the point of gaining this understanding is not to immediately dredge it up. That sort of thing will not only cause distress, but will raise understandable questions about how the patient's therapist could possibly know these things. Rather, the &quot;reading&quot; abilities serve as a way to coax the patient into talking, which is the true goal. The first step to resolving their problems is to bring them out into the open. Even just saying what is bothering them can be hugely beneficial to their emotional state, as venting is cathartic.<br /> <br /> <br /> Outside of the office, Mind 2 is very useful as part of the &quot;adventuring Mage lifestyle&quot;. The ability to tell truth from lies, to shield oneself from mind- or aura-reading, to multitask (while the character's actions are still limited in the physical speed of their body, they can have many mental processes working simultaneously), and the ability to keep a &quot;sense hostility&quot; Effect running in the background to warn of danger.<br /> <br /> Prime 1 can be used to &quot;consecrate&quot; personal objects. While this does infuse them with the mage's personal Resonance (and makes them count as a strong Correspondence connection), consecrated objects can &quot;carry with&quot; the mage when using Effects that non-bodily objects normally could not. (Shapeshifting, stepping sideways, etc). Prime 1 (or 2, I forget) has also been historically used to channel Quintessence from the mage's personal pattern, allowing them to sacrifice health for Quint on a one-for-one basis. It's a risky maneuver, &quot;casting from hit points&quot;, but it might be necessary in certain situations. It's good to have the <i>option</i>, at least.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T13:32:07-07:00","id":1336087,"title":"","content":"Well, yeah, there's a lot you can do with all three Spheres for this once they're higher.<br /> <br /> Though I'd suggest Entropy, and Life to add to the package at some point. Entropy has a lot of effects that can help a therapist (finding flaws and knowing if people are being truthful are both Entropy 1 effects). Life is a good supplement to Mind as trauma can impact both, as well, a lot of spiritual/supernatural badness in the WoD can literally harm people if you try to undo it (spirits possessing people tend to rip out of them painfully if you try to force them out), so some magical healing might be necessary if you need to deal with something ASAP and don't have time to slowly detach someone from the stuff haunting them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-16T17:35:35-07:00","id":1336124,"title":"","content":"Hey, thank you all for your replies, they have been very helpful to get me to think about how to use the spheres in the character's professional life. It makes sense I think that most of the usage amounts to subtle and helpful tricks to make her life and work easier so to speak considering that she is still &quot;just&quot; Arete 2 and thus just a dabbler in the magical world. I have no doubt that she will improve her Arete and sphere ratings as the story progess, she is just simply not quite there just yet. <br /> <br /> I agree that life and entropy is totally on the list of spheres to pick up down the line as well (entropy 1 and life 2 are just too damn useful to ignore). <br /> <br /> I think that it has been useful to consider how the spheres can be used and employed to help her in her life and general situations that may arise when you are a mage in the world of darkness as well as I doubt that she will be able to exclusively work from her own comfort zone haha. It seems like I am able to have my character strike so called spirit pacts with spirits with spirit 2, my question is what you could realistically expect from that? And that is of course ignoring the fact that dealing directly with spirits like that is an extremely dangerous thing to due, the faustian deal is a saying after all. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25626-eiryth","name":"Eiryth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25626_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-17T09:28:21-07:00","id":1336223,"title":"","content":"Also think about how your character does magic, as that will determine a lot about how she goes about using her magic to help people:<br /> <br /> Things like incense, hypnotism, and drugs are at least somewhat appropriate in a counselor's office. Your character can use them to ritually cast during counseling sessions without raising any eyebrows, which will let her choose her spells specifically for the person in front of her.<br /> <br /> If her instruments are odd but small, like sympathetic connections (using pieces of the target's hair or blood) and subtle but visible chiminage (offerings for spirits) she's can potentially hide what she's doing but risks scorn (or Paradox, depending on the spell) if she gets caught. Where possible she is going to want to use them out of the sight of her targets. She can probably risk fast spells without much of a problem (although at her Arete that won't do much) but ritual casting is a gamble. No one is going to question if she puts a little bird seed into a bowl once during a visit, especially if it is near an open window. It will be much more attention grabbing if she keeps filling bowls around her office throughout the entire hour. <br /> <br /> Anachronisms like blood sacrifices, chanting, or obvious rituals have to be kept out of sight, so your character will be limited in how often she can cast that way. Because she has to cast them further out from the time of use she's going to need to get more successes to keep the duration going. These spells can be tailored for specific patients, but are in general better suited for general effects that can increase her own abilities. A spell to make her able to hear lies would be much better than a spell to make a specific person <br /> <br /> Note that careful thought can negate a lot of these issues so don't feel too constrained. A lot of mages put in 'off screen' effort so it is quite possible for otherwise obvious anachronisms to be worked into her office in subtle ways. It's still something your character would have spent a lot of time working on so think of how it affects her approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T04:19:32-07:00","id":1336526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1335896-sphere-help?p=1336082#post1336082\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Once you raise your Prime to 3 you can get Quintessence from spirits, though usually it's best to get their permission first.</div> </div> </div> </div>Immortal enemies that you need to put effort into seeing and touching can be dangerous. So yeah, avoid pissing off spirits where possible. And if you do piss one off (I guess it's inevitable if you're using Spirit frequently) invest effort into protecting yourself. I'd imagine quite a few Mages would have a sort of &quot;spirit bodyguard&quot; who is bound to the Mage somehow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-18T16:40:56-07:00","id":1336700,"title":"","content":"I think the Spirit Quintessence thing also required like spirit 3/4 if using M20 (I think HDYDT or the chart says that? Idk) and it will probably piss them off, as already said.<br /> <br /> You do need Prime 3 if you want to 'accept' quintessence or 'give' it to other mages though, which sucks. Both of you have to have it. x.x (And before people start posting 'ACTHUALYL PRIME 0 IS ENOUGH BECAUSE I READ ONE THING' M20 literally states this in HDYDT and maybe in the regular book. So this is the assumption we are using those rules. Just saying 'I don't use that rule' is fine, because I don't either.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T06:02:34-07:00","id":1336849,"title":"","content":"To be fair, you have to be careful when using HDYDT as it is infamous for adding extra sphere requirements that make no sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-19T10:35:42-07:00","id":1336900,"title":"","content":"I've probably screamed about it before on here, so I'm very aware.<br /> <br /> Looking at you, Prime 2 Chi healing.<br /> <br /> That being said I'd probably make it Prime 4 for Ghosts/Spirits, atleast unwillingly. (The same way you turn inanimate objects into quintessence normally), or 3 if you accept it/they give it up.<br /> <br /> Then again theres like 50 optional rules on using Prime 3 (I think 3?) and 'stealing it' from people by doing interactions with them. Like: Torture, probably rape, sex but you spiritually take it from them, etc.<br /> <br /> It's strange.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25315-jihelu","name":"Jihelu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"167"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-09-21T06:31:45-07:00","id":1337241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ramnesis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1335896-sphere-help?p=1336849#post1336849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, you have to be careful when using HDYDT as it is infamous for adding extra sphere requirements that make no sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;If you want to do this easy effect in a much worse way, just add an irrelevant sphere and spend a bunch of Quintessence that you wouldn't need to otherwise&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}